WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:06.190
The hit Disney+ series The Mandalorian loves
to lob mystery after mystery at us with every

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:08.080
episode, and the fifth was no different.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:12.580
Case in point: Who the heck is the person
who discovers Fennec Shand's body at the end?

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:14.320
We can hazard a few guesses.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:19.300
The episode was something of a love letter
to Star Wars fans, as it returned us to where

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:24.140
it all started: the desert planet of Tatooine,
where "Mando" heads to get his ship repaired

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:27.520
after it sustains damage in a dogfight with
another bounty hunter.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.320
"Oh yeah, I'm gonna have to rotate that."

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:34.999
After leaving adorable lil' Baby Yoda in the
care of mechanic Peli Motto, Mando heads to

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.100
a very familiar cantina looking for work.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:42.160
There, he finds Toro Calican, a guild member
who just happens to be posted up at the very

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:47.060
same table where a certain Rodian bounty hunter
met his end so very long ago.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.640
He offers to split the take if Mando will
help him bring in his bounty: Fennec Shand,

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:55.340
a notorious assassin who has apparently made
enemies of the wrong people.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:58.740
Of course, it turns out that Calican isn't
telling the whole truth.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:03.139
He's not exactly a member of the guild, but
he sure wants to be, and hauling in Shand

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:03.980
is his ticket in.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:08.790
He offers to give Mando all of the dough to
assist in bringing in the extremely dangerous,

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:13.240
hardened killer and while our hero is just
a bit hesitant, well, money talks.

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:17.580
After meeting back at the mechanic's, the
two set out on speeder bikes, and it doesn't

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:22.030
take them long to find and corner Shand, who
puts up a heck of a fight, but is eventually

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:24.660
subdued by the power of deception and teamwork.

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:29.720
Unfortunately, Mando now has a bigger problem:
Shand, in attempting to convince Calican to

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:34.810
free her so they can team up to kill Mando
and get custody of Baby Yoda, instead convinces

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:38.080
him to blast her so that he can attempt the
double-cross on his own.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:41.600
This endeavor doesn't go well for the inexperienced
bounty hunter.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:46.120
After a confrontation back at the mechanic's,
Mando manages to get the better of Calican,

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:49.980
and use the credits he had on him to pay the
mechanic for his ship's repairs.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:54.140
He and Baby Yoda continue their flight but
somebody knows they've been there.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:59.300
We see Shand's (presumably) dead body being
approached and examined by an unknown party,

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:03.040
dressed all in black with a long, flowing
cape and what looks like a blaster on their

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:03.540
hip.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:05.420
Who this mysterious person?

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:06.760
We have a few ideas.

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:11.400
There is always the possibility that this
person will be one of the many bounty hunters

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:14.610
we've seen on Mando's trail over the course
of the season.

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:17.600
Baby Yoda is the hottest commodity in the
galaxy, after all.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:22.660
One such random pursuer made a surprise appearance
at the end of the previous episode, just when

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:26.060
we thought Mando might finally have found
a safe haven for Baby Yoda.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:30.090
So if he can be tracked to the remote outpost
of the planet Sorgan, he can certainly be

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:32.420
tracked to the comparative hot spot of Tatooine.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:37.020
However, we don't find this to be likely for
one simple reason: why not show the person's

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:37.520
face?

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:42.040
If he or she will indeed be another rando
in pursuit of Mando who will otherwise be

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:46.540
relatively unimportant to the plot, then there's
no real reason to conceal their identity.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:50.730
Sure, this party could very well be someone
we haven't gotten a formal introduction to

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:55.130
yet but it's probably someone who will play
a vital role in episodes to come, hence the

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:56.160
mysterious tease.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:03:00.640
Of course, the possibility also exists that
this is a character we have met before just

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:01.640
not in this series.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:06.860
The Mandalorian takes place five years after
the events of Star Wars: Return of the Jedi.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:11.000
And who has a loose but significant connection
to the Mandalorians, whom we last saw in that

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:15.100
film falling to his presumed death into the
gaping maw of the Sarlacc pit on Tatooine?

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:20.080
That's right: Boba Fett, whose armor differs
from Mando's only in color scheme and accessories,

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:25.660
and who, like Mando, isn't so much a Mandalorian
as he is a guy who really, really identifies

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:26.360
with the culture.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:31.080
Of course, it's up for debate whether Boba
actually survived his encounter with the Sarlacc.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:35.599
The extended Star Wars canon states so explicitly,
but the House of Mouse has been very, very

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:36.700
quiet on the matter.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:41.220
If indeed it was he who discovered Shand,
it would make sense to hide his helmeted dome

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:45.280
for a big reveal in another episode but, if
we're being honest, we're pretty sure that

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:46.280
this isn't the case.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:46.900
Here's why.

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:52.599
Thanks to Entertainment Weekly, we know that
Giancarlo Esposito's Moff Gideon is going

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:55.060
to be a major player in The Mandalorian's
narrative.

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:59.380
We're familiar with that "Moff" title; this
is an old Empire guy, obviously, but what

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:00.500
exactly is he after?

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:04.020
Esposito himself gave EW a few clues, saying,

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:09.200
"He's an Imperial remnant of a very fine officer
who then switches to become sort of the guardian

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:09.860
of the people.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:11.280
But what does he really want?

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:15.380
This guy is going to be a big player because
he has an idea of how to keep order."

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:20.019
That's an interesting statement, because so
far, the hunt for Mando has been pure chaos.

00:04:20.019 --> 00:04:24.100
The logline for an upcoming episode, though,
indicates that Gideon may have more on his

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:27.700
mind than simply bringing Baby Yoda in to
collect a bundle of cash.

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:32.120
We recently got a pretty strong indication
that The Mandalorian's seventh episode, which

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:36.610
drops Wednesday, December 18th, will bring
Gideon and Mando face-to-helmet.

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:37.600
The logline reads:

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:41.380
"An old rival extends an invitation for the
Mandalorian to make peace."

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:46.180
Sure, this could be referring to someone else
The Mandalorian is a show that loves to keep

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:46.820
us guessing.

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:50.880
Nevertheless, we're going to go ahead and
register our guess that the black-booted figure

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:54.400
seen crouching over Fennec Shand is indeed
Moff Gideon.

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:59.610
We can't wait to see Esposito make his Mandalorian
debut and to see what duplicitous schemes

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:01.520
his character might be cooking up.

